2.88.m:
The celestial lady said:
"This is indeed the ripening of my actions, O fortunate one, at present;
here I dwell in sorrow, accompanied by widowhood.

2.97.m:
Subāhu said:
"I shall perform dharma, I shall perform merit, O best of the twice-born;
I shall abundantly sacrifice to Vāsudeva, the source of the universe, O sage.

Direct that, O fortunate one; your word is authority for me.
Vāmadeva said:
The great praise of Vāsudeva destroys great sins;
